[0.010, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m  Diode Sentinel\u001b[0m  —  intrusion detection for strictly ONE-WAY traffic\r\n  PS-26145 · NTRO · the sensor sees one direction of every conversation.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[2m  no replies · no handshakes · no payload · no asking the network anything\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.005, "o", "\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m1. What the problem statement asks for — and what a diode can actually see\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.032, "o", "  21 PS features enumerated:  15 OBSERVABLE · 5 IMPOSSIBLE · 1 SUBSTITUTED\r\n\r\n    \u001b[31mIMPOSSIBLE\u001b[0m  round-trip time  (b)\r\n                 RTT requires the response; one-way latency is unmeasurable without a return path\r\n    \u001b[31mIMPOSSIBLE\u001b[0m  NXDOMAIN ratio  (c)\r\n                 RCODE lives in the DNS response header, which the diode never delivers\r\n    \u001b[31mIMPOSSIBLE\u001b[0m  JA3S / JA4S server fingerprint  (d)\r\n                 ServerHello is sent by the responder, which is not on the feed\r\n    \u001b[31mIMPOSSIBLE\u001b[0m  negotiated cipher / server certificate  (d)\r\n                 both are chosen by the responder after the handshake completes, off the observable path\r\n    \u001b[31mIMPOSSIBLE\u001b[0m  outbound-to-inbound byte ratio  (f)\r\n                 the inbound half of the flow is never seen, so the ratio has no denominator. The PS names a feature its own constraint (a) makes unsatisfiable\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1mFive of the statement's own requested features are ruled out by its own constraint.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
